      "content": "I see. To be more specific for my research, I'm looking for more granular distinctions. When we look at institutional settings—like emergency response or high-stakes corporate environments—is there a documented trend regarding which temperament is more \"effective\" or \"stable\"? For instance, does the tendency toward stoicism in East Asian cohorts lead to better leadership outcomes in crises, or does the more expressive/communal style in African cohorts provide better social cohesion in those same high-stress scenarios?",
